{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 64, :comments ["<b>And she saw Isaac and she fell from upon the camel.</b> She saw him majestic in stature, with a commanding face, walking across the fields with no road, for she was bashful. And she was young, three years old, and supposed he was an assailant or a bandit, and was alarmed and fell. Another interpretation: <b>and she fell from upon the camel</b> is inverted, coming after 'and she said to the servant.' And thus the interpretation of <b>and she saw Isaac</b> — 'and she said to the servant: who is that man walking in the field toward us?' And the servant said: 'he is my master.' And afterward: 'and she fell from upon the camel and took the veil and covered herself' — out of great modesty she threw herself down of her own will, like 'and he fell on his face.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The phrase 'ופרצוף מהלך' is taken as describing his commanding appearance as he walked; 'בעל קומה' as 'majestic in stature.' The phrase 'מסורס הוא אחר' means the verse order is inverted — the falling (v. 64) is placed after her dialogue with the servant (v. 65)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:45.482808020Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}